<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mountain Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1924">1924</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mountain ASSR, Gorskaya ASSR</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mountain Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic was an autonomous republic of the Russian SFSR in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, created in January 1921 with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a>. It united Chechen, Ingush, Ossetian, Kabardian, Balkar and Karachay districts. The Soviet government gradually detached its parts as separate autonomous regions and abolished it in 1924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mountain-autonomous-soviet-socialist-republic.jpg" alt="Mountain Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paolo Interdonato · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Mountain_ASSR_(1924_possible_reconstruction).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
